1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
世界，起初是一片数据。
In the beginning, the world is data.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
每一次点击，每一束光，每一个念头。
Every click. Every photon. Every idea.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
数量不是力量。组织，才是。
Volume is not power. Organization is.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
让关系显形，让计算发生。
Make relationships visible. Make computation possible.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
数据结构：数字世界的隐形建筑。
Data structures: the invisible architecture of our world.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
数组，让元素拥有连续的位置。
An array gives elements contiguous positions.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
基址加上偏移，直接抵达目标。
Base address plus offset. Arrive directly.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
按索引访问：O(1)。
Indexed access: O(1).

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
中间插入，通常需要移动后续元素。
Insertion in the middle usually shifts later elements.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
紧凑与局部性，让遍历更接近硬件的节奏。
Compact layout and locality bring traversal closer to hardware.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
链表，不要求相邻的内存。
A linked list does not require adjacent memory.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
每个节点，都保存通往下一个节点的线索。
Each node carries a reference to the next.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
已知插入位置，改写连接即可插入。
With the insertion position known, rewire the links.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
但寻找第 k 个节点，需要逐个前行。
Finding the kth node means following links one by one.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
灵活连接的代价：指针空间与访问局部性。
Flexibility costs pointer space and memory locality.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
栈，把最近发生的事留在顶端。
A stack keeps the most recent item on top.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
后进先出：LIFO。
Last in, first out: LIFO.

18
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
一次调用，压入一层上下文。
A call pushes another layer of context.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
一次返回，回到上一个现场。
A return restores the previous context.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
撤销、回溯、递归：秩序也可以向后。
Undo. Backtracking. Recursion. Order can run backward.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
队列，将到达顺序变成服务顺序。
A queue turns arrival order into service order.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
先进先出：FIFO。
First in, first out: FIFO.

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,000
尾部入队，头部出队。
Enqueue at the tail. Dequeue at the head.

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:24,000
广度优先搜索，一层一层探索未知。
Breadth-first search explores one layer at a time.

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
当生产快于消费，排队就成为延迟。
When production outpaces consumption, queues become latency.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
哈希函数，把键映射到桶。
A hash function maps a key to a bucket.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
理想的分布，让查找平均接近 O(1)。
Good distribution enables expected O(1) lookup.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
不同的键，也可能落入同一个桶。
Different keys can land in the same bucket.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
冲突必须处理，扩容也有成本。
Collisions need a strategy. Resizing has a cost.

30
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
平均很快，不意味着最坏情况也很快。
Fast on average does not mean fast in the worst case.

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
树，将关系组织成层次。
A tree organizes relationships into a hierarchy.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,000
二叉搜索树，让比较决定向左还是向右。
A binary search tree turns comparison into direction.

33
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
保持平衡，查找路径可缩短到 O(log n)。
With balance, search paths can be O(log n).

34
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:24,000
失去平衡，树也可能退化成一条链。
Without balance, a tree can degenerate into a chain.

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,000
层次的力量，来自持续维护的约束。
The power of hierarchy comes from maintained invariants.

36
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
当关系不再是一条线，也不再是一棵树。
When relationships are neither a line nor a tree.

37
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
顶点与边，构成网络。
Vertices and edges form a network.

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
道路、依赖、社交：同一种抽象。
Roads. Dependencies. Social ties. One abstraction.

39
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,000
遍历让连接可见，路径让距离可计算。
Traversal reveals connections. Paths make distance computable.

40
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
图不只记录世界，也让我们探索世界。
Graphs do not just record the world. They let us explore it.

41
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
同一份数据，可以拥有不同的组织方式。
The same data can take different forms.

42
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
时间、空间、局部性、维护成本。
Time. Space. Locality. Maintenance.

43
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:18,000
大 O 描述增长趋势，不是实际耗时。
Big O describes growth, not elapsed time.

44
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
读多还是写多？数据多大？操作是什么？
Read-heavy or write-heavy? How much data? Which operations?

45
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
最好的结构，来自对问题的深刻理解。
The best structure begins with understanding the problem.

46
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
数组赋予位置，链表赋予连接。
Arrays give position. Linked lists give connection.

47
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
栈保存来路，队列安排前行。
Stacks remember the way back. Queues arrange the way forward.

48
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,000
哈希加速抵达，树缩小选择，图连接世界。
Hashes locate. Trees narrow. Graphs connect.

49
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
算法决定如何前进，结构决定如何组织。
Algorithms decide how to proceed. Structures decide how to organize.

50
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
理解结构，创造可能。
Understand structure. Create possibility.
